<div class="game-item-card" id="gic-<%= item.id %>">
    <div class="game-item-img-wrap">
        <% if (item.hasImage) { %>
            <img
                class="game-item-img"
                id="gic-img-<%= item.id %>"
                src="/api/v1/item-image/activity/<%= guild.id %>/<%= item.id %>"
                alt=""
                <%# If the upload 404s, the image hides itself and the emoji
                    below takes its place. guild-settings.js listens for the
                    error in the capture phase (#887); `error` does not bubble,
                    and an on* attribute is what the CSP no longer allows. -%>
                data-emoji-fallback="gic-emoji-<%= item.id %>"
            >
            <span class="game-item-emoji" id="gic-emoji-<%= item.id %>" style="display:none"><%= item.emoji %></span>
        <% } else { %>
            <span class="game-item-emoji" id="gic-emoji-<%= item.id %>"><%= item.emoji %></span>
        <% } %>
    </div>
    <div class="game-item-info">
        <div class="game-item-name"><%= item.label %></div>
        <div class="game-item-id"><%= item.id %></div>
    </div>
    <div class="game-item-actions">
        <%# The input is clipped, not hidden (#880). `display: none` took it out
            of the tab order, and a <label> is not a tab stop of its own — which
            left no way at all to reach this control without a mouse. `.sr-only`
            keeps it invisible and focusable, and styles.css puts the focus ring
            on the label so it lands on the thing that is actually on screen.

            The name is per-item because every card here says "Upload": a screen
            reader listing the page's controls would otherwise read out a column
            of sixty-odd identical buttons. The id is in it as well as the
            label, because three item names ("Repair Kit (Small)", "XP Scroll")
            are shared by the hunt, fish and mine catalogues and the id is what
            tells those apart — on the card it is the line under the name. -%>
        <label class="btn btn-sm btn-primary game-item-upload-btn" title="Upload image">
            Upload
            <input
                type="file"
                class="sr-only"
                aria-label="Upload an image for <%= item.label %> (<%= item.id %>)"
                accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/gif,image/webp"
                data-change="activity-image-upload" data-item-id="<%= item.id %>"
            >
        </label>
        <button class="btn btn-sm btn-danger" data-action="activity-image-remove" data-item-id="<%= item.id %>" title="Remove image" aria-label="Remove the image for <%= item.label %> (<%= item.id %>)">✕</button>
    </div>
</div>
